,19788,10374,13233,90,64,92,1124,15136,1124,10374,13233,90,65,38842,59,60,2870,57960,10374,13233,90,64,31716,374,264,4982,4621,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Find the maximum value of\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}),\\]where $\\mathbf{a}$ is a unit vector.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"19d818f8ecdfc25e423979565165654df309e6994d6190fc58c5abe6c8e7304c"},"seconds":40.47204828262329,"seed":955109446245264259,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the maximum value of the scalar triple product \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\), where \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is a unit vector.\n\nFirst, recall that the scalar triple product \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) represents the volume of the parallelepiped formed by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\). This product can also be written as the determinant of the matrix formed by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\).\n\nSince \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is a unit vector, the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is maximized when \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) is perpendicular to \\(\\mathbf{b}\\). The magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is then equal to the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), which is \\(\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|\\).\n\nThe magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-1)^2 + 4^2 + 6^2} = \\sqrt{1 + 16 + 36} = \\sqrt{53}.\n\\]\n\nThe maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is achieved when \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is parallel to \\(\\mathbf{c}\\), and the value is the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) times the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{b}\\). Therefore, we need to calculate \\(\\|\\mathbf{c}\\|\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| = \\sqrt{2^2 + (-7)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 100} = \\sqrt{153}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is the product of the magnitudes of \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{c}\\| \\cdot \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{153} \\cdot \\sqrt{53} = \\sqrt{153 \\cdot 53} = \\sqrt{8109}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of \\(\\mathbf{c} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b})\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{8109}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\sqrt{8109}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
